[BLAME] benchmark_1/parts/task_queue/lib/task_worker_impl.py: In lib/task_worker_impl.py, fetch_and_execute (lines 88-104) violates the GROUNDING of low/task_worker_impl.pyi: after queue.dispatch() succeeds it must call self.execute(task_id, payload) and only then return the task identifier. The method currently returns the dispatched task_id without invoking self.execute, so none of the contracted execution effects happen: queue.complete is never called, _last_task_id stays None, _processed_count is not incremented, and the busy-state transition in execute is skipped. After a successful dispatch the observed postcondition is last_task_id None and processed_count 0, whereas the specification requires the dispatched task to be fully executed before its identifier is returned.
