[BLAME] benchmark_1/parts/task_queue/pretense/task_queue_pretense.py: TaskQueueStateMachine.dispatch (lines 79-92) pops the pending head but fails to model the completion notification that a dispatch must trigger: the queue's dispatch contract executes the popped task through the worker, and the worker's execute contract requires a successful execution to notify the queue of completion with the computed outcome, so a dispatched task carries a recorded outcome immediately after dispatch. Because the transition leaves the model's recorded outcomes unchanged, the model's get_outcome transition (lines 112-121) computes a stale expected value and its postcondition assertion fails against the realized PROCESSED-prefixed outcome, both in stateful fuzzing and in the real conformance path. The dispatch transition must record the completion outcome produced for the dispatched task so the model's outcome expectations track the queue's realized outcome map.
[BLAME] benchmark_1/parts/task_queue/pretense/task_worker_impl_pretense.py: TestTaskWorkerImplReal.test_real_conformance (lines 143-160) and the TaskWorkerFuzzTest SUT factory make_sut (lines 180-186) leave the collaborator task queue unseeded. The worker's fetch_and_execute contract returns the identifier of the task dispatched from the collaborator queue and requires WorkerError when the collaborator has zero pending tasks, so the fuzz factory must seed the collaborator queue (or declare the task queue state machine in compile_hypothesis_test_case) so that a drawn fetch_and_execute has a pending task; otherwise the drawn call raises the contracted WorkerError, a *Error the fuzz run cannot handle, which is the observed crash. Likewise the real conformance scenario must seed the collaborator queue with the specific dispatched task identifier that the state machine's fetch_and_execute expectation returns, since the checked call compares that expectation against the realized dispatch identifier and currently mismatches.
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/task_queue/pretense/task_queue_pretense.py: Fix dispatch model to record the dispatched task's completion outcome (PROCESSED:<payload.upper()>), keeping get_outcome expectations aligned with the queue's realized outcome map in fuzzing and real conformance; update fake coverage assertions.
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/task_queue/pretense/task_worker_impl_pretense.py: Fix worker fetch_and_execute: gate planned dispatch on the collaborator queue's pending_count so exploratory fuzzing never invokes the contracted WorkerError path, and seed the real conformance queue with the expected dispatched id 'dispatched-task' so the checked expectation matches the realized identifier.
[CLEAN] benchmark_1/parts/task_queue/pretense/task_queue_impl_pretense.py
[BLAME] benchmark_1/parts/task_queue/pretense/task_queue_impl_pretense.py: TestTaskQueueImplReal.test_real_conformance (lines 208-213) drives the unavailable-path submit, dispatch, and complete calls directly through the checked target while relying on the transition-body raises(...) expectation to consume the contracted QueueUnavailableException. Checked dispatch executes the transition body directly, so that expectation is not consumed and the contracted QueueUnavailableException propagates out of the checked submit call at line 210 and would likewise propagate from the checked dispatch and complete calls at lines 211-212, erroring the scenario before the unavailable-path post-conditions are observed. Per the queue contract, submit, dispatch, and complete MUST raise QueueUnavailableException when the queue is unavailable, so the real conformance scenario must declare that expected exception for those checked calls; the previous change added unavailable-path coverage and corrected the model dispatch outcome recording, but it did not declare the expected exception on the checked unavailable-path calls, so those checked calls still error.
[BLAME] benchmark_1/parts/task_queue/pretense/task_worker_impl_pretense.py: TestTaskWorkerImplReal.test_real_conformance (lines 175-180) drives a failing-task execute directly through the checked target while relying on the transition-body raises(...) expectation to consume the contracted WorkerExecutionException. Checked dispatch executes the transition body directly, so that expectation is not consumed and the contracted WorkerExecutionException propagates out of the checked execute call at line 177, erroring the scenario before the busy-state and processed-count post-conditions at lines 178-180 are observed. Per the worker contract, execute MUST raise WorkerExecutionException when execution fails, so the real conformance scenario must declare that expected exception for the checked failing-task call; the previous change gated exploratory fuzzing and seeded the collaborator queue in the checked setup, but it left this real-conformance failure path without an expected-exception declaration, so the checked call still errors.
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/task_queue/pretense/task_queue_impl_pretense.py: Declare the contracted QueueUnavailableException on the checked unavailable-path submit/dispatch/complete calls in TestTaskQueueImplReal so the scenario observes the unavailable-postconditions instead of erroring.
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/task_queue/pretense/task_worker_impl_pretense.py: Declare the contracted WorkerExecutionException on the checked failing-task execute call in TestTaskWorkerImplReal so the scenario observes the busy-state and processed-count postconditions instead of erroring.
